From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:53:33 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: vc1: check the picture data offset against the payload

The picture header is skipped with one bit reader access per 24 bits of
data_bit_offset, each followed by a busy wait of up to 1 ms. The offset
was not checked: a value near U32_MAX kept the decoding job in this loop
for millions of iterations. An Advanced profile payload shorter than its
start code also made the bitstream length underflow.

Reject both before the engine is enabled.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c   | 25 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
index 85538d9c3..31977543e 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
@@ -451,6 +451,7 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 	u32 reg, condover, pq;
 	struct vb2_queue *vq;
 	size_t buf_size;
+	u64 payload_bits;
 	bool advanced;
 	int brfd, flag;
 
@@ -534,6 +535,18 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 			vb2_find_buffer(vq, picture->backward_ref_ts) : NULL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * An Advanced profile buffer begins with the frame or field start code
+	 * (00 00 01 0D/0C), which data_bit_offset does not count. The picture
+	 * data must start inside the payload: the header is skipped one bit
+	 * reader access per 24 bits below.
+	 */
+	sc_offset = advanced ? VC1_START_CODE_BITS : 0;
+	payload_bits = (u64)vb2_get_plane_payload(src_buf, 0) * 8;
+	if (payload_bits < sc_offset ||
+	    picture->data_bit_offset > payload_bits - sc_offset)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	cedrus_engine_enable(ctx);
 
 	/*
@@ -586,15 +599,11 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 	 */
 	buf_size = vb2_plane_size(src_buf, 0);
 	/*
-	 * An Advanced profile buffer begins with the frame or field start code
-	 * (00 00 01 0D/0C), which data_bit_offset does not count. Start the
-	 * bit reader after it: with start-code detection enabled, reading over
-	 * a start code with GET_BITS desyncs the VLD (every picture failed on
-	 * H616).
+	 * Start the bit reader after the start code of an Advanced profile
+	 * buffer: with start-code detection enabled, reading over a start code
+	 * with GET_BITS desyncs the VLD (every picture failed on H616).
 	 */
-	sc_offset = advanced ? VC1_START_CODE_BITS : 0;
-	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_BITS_LEN,
-		     vb2_get_plane_payload(src_buf, 0) * 8 - sc_offset);
+	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_BITS_LEN, payload_bits - sc_offset);
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_BITS_OFFSET, sc_offset);
 
 	src_buf_addr = vb2_dma_contig_plane_dma_addr(src_buf, 0);
-- 
